  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency response to Cyclone-Affected Populations in Vanuatu with lifesaving Shelter and Non-Food Items (ES/NFI)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The objective of project is to improve the living conditions of cyclone-affected people by providing Shelter and Non-Food Items (S/NFI), monitoring displaced populations, and assisting evacuation centres in target provinces. This IOM project activities include procuring/distributing S/NFI kits to beneficiary households, tracking displacement data, producing displacement reports, sharing information with government/humanitarian partners, identifying/referring gaps in service provision and advocating for partner response. The project provides life-saving assistance to 2,760 people, including 856 men, 839 women, 539 boys, 526 girls, and 40 persons with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
